@page


<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />

    <title>Student Study Planner | Muhammad Ishaq</title>

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="~/css/style.css">
</head>

<body>
    <header>
        <nav>
            <h2>Muhammad Ishaq</h2>

            <a href="index.html">Back to Portfolio</a>
        </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
        <section class="case-study-hero">
            <p class="section-label">CASE STUDY / 01</p>

            <h1>Student Study Planner</h1>

            <p>
                A productivity web application designed to help students organize,
                manage and track their study tasks.
            </p>

            <div class="case-study-preview">
                <img src="~/images/student-study-planner.png" alt="Student Study Planner application" />
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="case-study-section">
            <p class="section-label">THE PROBLEM</p>

            <h2>Students need a simple way to stay organized.</h2>

            <p>
                Managing multiple study tasks can become difficult when deadlines,
                priorities and completed work are not organized in one place.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="case-study-section">
            <p class="section-label">THE GOAL</p>

            <h2>Create a simple study management tool.</h2>

            <p>
                The goal was to create a practical web application that allows
                students to add tasks, set priorities and due dates, track progress
                and manage completed work.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="case-study-section">
            <p class="section-label">THE SOLUTION</p>

            <h2>A focused task management experience.</h2>

            <p>
                I built a browser-based study planner with task management,
                priorities, due dates, filters, search and local storage.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="case-study-section">
            <p class="section-label">KEY FEATURES</p>
            <h2>Built around the everyday study workflow.</h2>

            <div class="features-grid">
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h3>Task Management</h3>
                    <p>Add, complete and delete study tasks.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h3>Priorities</h3>
                    <p>Organize tasks according to importance.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h3>Due Dates</h3>
                    <p>Track deadlines and identify overdue tasks.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h3>Search & Filters</h3>
                    <p>Find tasks and filter active or completed work.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="case-study-section">
            <p class="section-label">WHAT I LEARNED</p>

            <h2>Building functionality from the ground up.</h2>

            <p>
                This project helped me understand JavaScript fundamentals, DOM
                manipulation, events, arrays, functions, local storage and building
                interactive user interfaces.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="case-study-back">
            <a href="index.html">← Back to Portfolio</a>
        </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
        <p>© 2026 Muhammad Ishaq. All rights reserved.</p>
    </footer>
</body>

</html>
